  "rationale": "**Holds.** `run_auto_sync` returns `!session_start` after a successful non-`SessionStart` sync: it re-synced because the freshness gate was not satisfied. `execute_hook` passes that to `dispatch_builtin`. For `PostToolUse` and `UserPromptSubmit` it goes through `handle_post_tool_use` / `handle_user_prompt_submit` to `possible_new_plugins_notice`, which, when `notify` is true, returns context saying there may be new agent plugins and telling the agent to \"tell the user to run `cargo agents sync`... Do not enable them yourself\".\n\n**Tests (pass):** `tests/plugin_notice.rs::a_dependency_added_by_a_tool_call_is_noticed_once` (after `SessionStart`, a dependency is added and the next Claude `PostToolUse` carries the notice; later events do not), `a_dependency_the_user_added_is_noticed_with_their_next_prompt` (`UserPromptSubmit`), `agents_that_read_context_after_a_tool_call_get_the_notice` (Codex, Copilot, Kiro). The unit tests `builtin_post_tool_use_returns_empty_when_dependencies_are_unchanged` and `builtin_user_prompt_submit_returns_empty_when_dependencies_are_unchanged` cover the `notify = false` side.\n\nNote: because the gate also fails when no sync is recorded (see `auto_sync_gate`), the notice also appears on the first such event in a directory with no recorded sync. That is extra, not a violation of this MUST.\n",
  "requirement": "On `PostToolUse` and `UserPromptSubmit` right after auto-sync re-synced because a package-manager input changed, Symposium MUST add context telling the agent to point the user at `cargo agents sync`."
}
